# Design System — Use It, Don't Reinvent It

The app is **dark-theme only**. All colors are CSS custom properties in `:root` in
[app/javascript/entrypoints/application.css](app/javascript/entrypoints/application.css).

## Critical: there are NO semantic Tailwind color utilities

Colors are plain CSS variables, **not** `@theme` tokens. The only `@theme` entry is `--font-sans`.
So `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `border-border` **do not exist and will silently render nothing**.

Reference tokens with Tailwind's arbitrary-value syntax instead:

```tsx
// BAD — these utilities are not generated
<div className="bg-card text-foreground border-border">
<div className="bg-blue-500 text-gray-400">        // raw palette ignores the theme
<div className="bg-[#1b1f26]">                      // hard-coded hex

// GOOD — the established idiom
<div className="bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)]">
<span className="text-[var(--foreground-muted)]">
<div className="bg-[var(--accent)]/14 border-[var(--accent)]/20">   // opacity suffix is fine
```

## Available tokens

Surfaces: `--background`, `--background-sidebar`, `--background-secondary`, `--background-subtle`,
`--background-elevated`, `--card`, `--card-hover`
Text: `--foreground`, `--foreground-muted`, `--foreground-subtle`
Brand: `--primary`, `--primary-hover`, `--primary-foreground`, `--accent`, `--accent-hover`
Secondary: `--secondary`, `--secondary-hover`, `--secondary-foreground`
Borders/inputs: `--border`, `--border-strong`, `--input-border`, `--input`, `--input-focus`
Status: `--success`, `--success-muted`, `--success-background`, `--success-text`, `--error`,
`--error-muted`, `--warning`, `--warning-muted`
Focus: `--ring`, `--ring-offset` · Shadows: `--shadow-sm`, `--shadow-md`, `--shadow-lg`

If a color you need has no token, **ask before adding one** — don't inline a hex value.

## Reuse components before writing markup

Check [app/javascript/components/ui/index.ts](app/javascript/components/ui/index.ts) first. Existing:
`Button`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Card` (+`CardHeader/Content/Footer/Title`), `Badge`, `Table`
(+`TableHeader/Body/Row/Head/Cell`), `TableEmpty`, `List`/`ListSection`/`ListItem`, `TabBar`,
`SearchInput`, `SlideOver` (+`Header/Section/CloseButton/FooterButtons`), `FooterActions`,
`ProgressBar`, `DotPattern`, `PasswordRequirements`.

Use existing variants rather than overriding with `className`:

- `Button`: `variant` `'primary' | 'secondary' | 'ghost' | 'destructive'`, `size` `'sm' | 'md' | 'lg'`,
  plus `loading`, `icon`, `iconPosition`, `fullWidth`, `asChild`
- `Badge`: `variant` `'default' | 'draft' | 'approved' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'error' | 'bounced' | 'info' | 'purple' | 'not-started' | 'in-sequence' | 'replied' | 'meeting-set' | 'outline' | 'cyan'`
- `Input`: `label`, `description`, `error` (`string | string[]`), `icon`, `size`, `containerClassName`

Note there is **no Modal/Dialog** — the established pattern for overlays is `SlideOver`.

## Class composition

There is **no `cn()` helper** and neither `clsx` nor `tailwind-merge` is installed. Components build
classes with arrays joined by spaces, then append the incoming `className` last:

```tsx
const allClasses = [baseClasses, variantClasses, sizeClasses, className].filter(Boolean).join(' ')
```

Don't add a class-merging dependency without asking.

## Radius, scrollbars

Buttons use `rounded-xl`, badges `rounded-full`, cards/inputs `rounded-lg`/`rounded-md`.
For scrollable regions use the existing `.custom-scrollbar` / `.custom-scrollbar-skinny` classes.
